The pass that prepares a 16 KiB-signed image for the 4 KiB kernel, on every processor.

launchd registers the 82 files of the dyld shared cache (6873 MiB) one after the other before the first daemon
starts, and the kernel reads each to its code limit and hashes it twice in that one thread: about 30 s of every
boot at 225 MiB/s, storage taking about 2 s of it. For an image above 32 MiB the caller now shares the chunks
with one helper thread per further processor. Each thread reads into a buffer of its own, authenticates every
16 KiB block against the code directory and derives the 4 KiB hashes from the same bytes, as before; the first
error ends the pass, nothing is published unless every block passed, and the table is made read-only before
the blob is visible. Smaller images are prepared by the caller alone.

Has not run on hardware.
